// The two measurements the chrome is built from, both in design pixels times the
// UI scale.
//
// A pane header is 13 design pixels: an 8-pixel glyph with two above and three
// below. A list row is 10: the glyph plus one either side. Naming them means a
// change to the type size moves the chrome with it, and means neither number is
// a bare literal at a dozen call sites (NAMES.md §5).

// Both are the glyph's height plus padding, not a constant that happened to suit
// an 8-pixel face. The face is loadable now and the default is 16 rows tall, so
// a bar of 13 design pixels was shorter than the text in it and a row of 10 was
// shorter than the row below it -- the hierarchy pane's lines overlapped.
//
// The padding is what is chosen here: five pixels of a bar, two of a list row,
// both scaled with the type like everything else in the chrome.
ed_hdr() {
} return int (txt_cellh() + 5) * txt_ui();

ed_rowh() {
} return int (txt_cellh() + 2) * txt_ui();
